==Strategy==
After [[Caliban's Keeper]] got demolished on every difficulty via [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless]] power creep, it went to Hell and got [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] and [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] enemies. This both helps and hurts the stage from being a true menace: on one hand, Oldstrich is painful to deal with, and The Thrillerz burrowing disrupts your meatshield flow from reaching the frontline. On another hand, Coffin Zoge gives you a free stepping stone. In this stage are also Mooth, who dies to anything and helps out by giving you a bucketload of cash, and Rain D. who's here to be annoying as hell. [[Talents|Talented]] [[Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can kill Rain D. quickly, or you can abuse Coffin Zoge to get [[Housewife Cat]] and [[Hitman Cat]] to kill Rain D. From there, it's really just spamming [[:Category:Cats with Freeze Immunity|Freeze-immune units]] and your typical Oldstrich counters like [[Shigong Cat]] and [[Fried Chicken Cat]] to win. If you got Shigong's Freeze Resist Talent for whatever reason, this stage should be incredibly easy.

This stage can be rushed before the Oldstrich appears, using Talented Awakened Bahamut Cat. The Thrillerz will slow you down, so it is wise to also deploy lots of [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCats]] to clear the way. Any other attackers that can help remove Rain D. and attack the base are also useful, especially if they happen to be [[Immune to Freeze]].

